  acral cases identified: 0 | mucosal: 0 | Skin NOS (uninformative): 318 
  [FLAG] NO acral or mucosal case is identifiable from this column. 
  The site adjustment below therefore CANNOT address the acral 
  confound; it only separates skin from lymph node and other. Any 
  verdict must say so. The informative test is the one restricted 
  to UV-POSITIVE tumours in 39b (rho -0.120, p = 0.033, n = 320), 
  which is a gradient by degree of UV damage among UV-exposed 
  melanomas rather than a contrast between exposed and shielded 
  sites. 
  informative for the acral/mucosal question: 11 of 411 (3%) 
  [FLAG] fewer than half the samples carry an informative site. 
  TCGA records many melanomas as 'Skin, NOS', so the adjustment 
  below is limited and the verdict may be UNRESOLVED. That is a 
  real answer about the metadata, not a failure of the analysis. 

