== 6. Verdict against the pre-set criterion ==================== 
  SITE-INDEPENDENT = UV effect keeps > 60% with site in the model at 
                     p < 0.05, AND holds within cutaneous only 
  SITE-CONFOUNDED  = loses more than that, or significance 
  UNRESOLVED       = site data too coarse to decide 
 
  RASSF9 vs UV burden: UNRESOLVED for acral/mucosal -- no such case is identifiable in the metadata; see the UV-positive-only test in 39b 
    unadjusted -0.0852 -> with site -0.0849 (100% retained, p = 0.001) 
    cutaneous only: n = 329, rho = -0.178, p = 0.001 
 
  RASSF10 vs UV burden: UNRESOLVED for acral/mucosal -- no such case is identifiable in the metadata; see the UV-positive-only test in 39b 
    unadjusted -0.1537 -> with site -0.1475 (96% retained, p = 8.68e-07) 
    cutaneous only: n = 329, rho = -0.255, p = 2.90e-06 
 
  A caution on over-adjustment: if UV burden is largely a CONSEQUENCE 
  of where a melanoma arose, then site sits on the causal path rather 
  than beside it, and adjusting for it removes real signal along with 
  the confound. Surviving adjustment is therefore strong evidence; 
  failing it is not proof that the association is spurious. The 
  cutaneous-only analysis is the cleaner test for that reason. 
